          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "Transport for a Bitcoin price-forecasting app: public market-data polling every ~9 minutes (grabber.py loop writes dataset.csv) and per-prediction current-price fetches (util.getCurrentData/getCEXData, driven from network.py's predictFuture loop). TLS posture is entirely library defaults: no custom SSLContext, no cipher/group list, no CA pinning, certificate verification left ON — so the key exchange is whatever the deployment's OpenSSL negotiates, at minimum classical ECDHE, with hybrid X25519M"
